{"task":"Migrate an older config without reinstalling","goals":"Give a pulled update a one-command path that is not the full installer","status":"Waiting","recorded_at":"2026-09-10T03:32:00Z","body":"There was no update path. Pulling a new ldev left the config as whatever an older version\nwrote, and the only remedy anywhere in the tool was one line in doctor telling you to re-run\ninstall.sh — which asks every question again, wants sudo, reinstalls the launchd daemon and\noffers to tear down whatever is currently serving. That is the wrong shape for \"a release\nadded a key\".\n\nWorse, the drift was invisible. Every use site reads its value as ${X:-default}, which keeps\nan old config working — correctly — and also means a key added two releases ago is silently\nabsent everywhere and its owner is never once asked about the choice it represents. This\nmachine was in exactly that state: PROXY_FALLBACK missing, everything behaving plausibly.\n\nSo the keys this version expects are now declared in one place, CONFIG_KEYS, rather than\nimplied by a scattered default at each use, and CONFIG_OBSOLETE names the ones older\nversions wrote that this one does not understand. Those are inert if left, but they describe\na machine that no longer exists — MODE=persite on an install with no per-site mode is a lie a\nfuture reader will believe.\n\n`ldev update` adds what is missing, removes what is obsolete, and leaves values alone. That\nlast part is the whole difference between a migration and a reinstall: ADMIN_PORT=2021 is on\nthis machine precisely because 2019 was taken, and a migration that resets it re-creates the\ncollision somebody fixed by hand. The previous file is copied to config.bak-<timestamp>\nfirst, and a second run does nothing and says so.\n\nTwo things it reports rather than does, both root-owned: a launchd plist that differs from\nthis version's template, and no daemon installed at all. Saying nothing about the first would\nbe worse than either — a daemon still running last release's template is the kind of drift\nthat survives every other check in the tool. install.sh remains the right answer whenever\nsudo is genuinely needed; update is for the far commoner case where it is not.\n\ndoctor gained the matching check, so the drift is reported where people already look rather\nthan only when they think to run update.\n\nVerified against this machine, which had the drift for real: doctor named the missing key,\nupdate added PROXY_FALLBACK=no and left ADMIN_PORT=2021 alone, doctor went green, and a\nsecond update reported it was already current.\n\ntest/update.test.sh covers a config written by an older ldev — MODE present, newer keys\nabsent — asserting that the new key is added, MODE is removed, a hand-set port and the sites\ndirectory survive, the backup holds the pre-migration content, a second run changes nothing\nand writes no second backup, doctor reports the drift and names the fix, and a key that\nexists but is empty is left alone. That last one draws the boundary deliberately: update\nfills missing keys, it does not police values.\n","parent_commit":"8741fd6fb835569633813ff46fc016a1a3a3b34f","repo":"brave-cedar-fb33","pct":"67","tasks":[{"id":"schema","content":"Declare CONFIG_KEYS and CONFIG_OBSOLETE in one place instead of implying them from scattered defaults","status":"completed"},{"id":"update-cmd","content":"ldev update: add missing keys, drop obsolete ones, leave set values alone, back up first","status":"completed"},{"id":"plist","content":"Report a launchd plist that differs from this version's template, rather than silently running last release's","status":"completed"},{"id":"doctor","content":"doctor reports config drift and names ldev update","status":"completed"},{"id":"tests","content":"test/update.test.sh — 12 assertions over migration, idempotence, backup and the doctor hint","status":"completed","created_at":"2026-09-10T01:14:35.832Z","status_at":"2026-09-10T01:14:35.832Z"},{"id":"docs","content":"README: the Updating section, the contents entry, the commands and tests listings","status":"completed","created_at":"2026-09-10T03:09:42.808Z","status_at":"2026-09-10T03:09:42.808Z"},{"id":"dup","content":"Reconcile with claude/lucid-ember-7451, which rebuilt the free-port and root-Caddy detection independently","status":"pending","human_reason":"That branch's e8f7051 duplicates ed06eca and b167a1c duplicates ae17bec, both in install.sh and both now on master. Two sessions solved the same two problems in the same file, so landing that branch will conflict and one implementation has to be chosen. Which to keep is Bryce's call; I could not identify the peer session reliably enough to message it without risking the wrong one.","created_at":"2026-09-10T03:09:42.808Z","status_at":"2026-09-10T03:09:42.808Z"},{"id":"triaj-swap","content":"Retire sh.brew.caddy so ldev can own 443, now that triaj.ldev is a proxy site","status":"pending","human_reason":"Needs sudo and a terminal, which this session has neither of. triaj.ldev is now a proxy site pointing at the same 127.0.0.1:5273 the Homebrew caddy proxies to, so the swap no longer breaks it — but stopping sh.brew.caddy and installing com.ldev.caddy is root-owned and briefly takes triaj.ldev and matsu.ldev offline. Re-run install.sh; it finds sh.brew.caddy by reading the config it runs and offers to take it down.","created_at":"2026-09-10T03:09:42.808Z","status_at":"2026-09-10T03:09:42.808Z"},{"id":"rehome-run","content":"Run ldev rehome against seasonal-drops","status":"pending","human_reason":"Rewrites live site data: 16,224 database rows plus WP_HOME/WP_SITEURL in wp-config.php. The command refuses to run without a terminal to confirm on. Do it after the swap, since the portless URL only works once the wildcard daemon owns 443.","created_at":"2026-09-09T19:22:30.481Z","status_at":"2026-09-09T19:22:30.481Z"}],"agent":"claude-code","changelog":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","code_quality":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).